{#
  The escape route upward, wherever a reader actually landed.

  Nineteen of the thirty-one guidance pages once had no inbound link from outside their own
  collection, so a reader arriving from a search engine had no way to discover anything else
  existed (KI-WEBSITE-SITE-019). The answer was a link up to whatever the page belonged to.

  That used to be the project a guide described, because guides lived under their projects. They
  now live in Docs sections, so the way up is the section — which is also what the reader is
  working through (KI-WEBSITE-SITE-037). `section` is set by the directory data file beside the
  pages, so the link is derived from where a page lives rather than from a line each page
  repeats.
#}
{%- if section %}
  {%- set label = '' %}
  {%- for entry in docsSections %}{% if entry.slug == section %}{% set label = entry.title %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}

<p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><a href="/docs/">← Docs</a>{% if label %} · {{ label }}{% endif %}</p>

{%- endif %}
